  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Flood Relief support to families affected by floods in Sri Lanka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Heavy inter monsoonal rains since the early morning of 16/05/16 have affected several parts of the country. Floods, landslides and strong winds have led to the displacement of several thousands of families. According to the Disaster Management Centre (DMC) as of 1300 hrs on 18/5/16, 82,924 families consisting of 352,374 persons have been affected while 48,998 families consisting of 223,687 persons are staying in 375 safe locations. 37 persons have died so far while 21 persons are missing. The no of people dead is likely to increase as reports come in of further landslides. 229houses have been completely damaged while 2,2,647 houses are reported as partially damaged. 

Caritas Sri Lanka have launched an Rapid One Month Emergency Appeal to reach 6,300 families (26,460 people) across 7 districts with food and NFIs.

Initially a one month project, this has been extended by 3 weeks and revised budget, logframe and explanations have been circulated.</narrative>
  </description>
